        "text": "Prior/update/interval: use a 12-month same-series persistence/base-rate model comprising 12 monthly ABS seasonally adjusted total-dwellings levels and their 11 successive changes from June 2025 through May 2026. The changes have a 1.4% mean and sample sigma = 18.3 percentage points. Starting from the 1.4% historical mean, apply roughly +1.0 point for rebound after May weakness, -0.5 point for the mildly negative trend, and -0.4 point for continued multi-unit normalization, yielding 1.5% after rounding. The normal-reference 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 1.28*18.3 = 23.4 points, so 1.5 \u00b1 23.4 gives -21.9% to 24.9%, rounded outward to -22% and 25%."
